| Middle of a three-level chain: the test links THIS file, and this file
| links base_chain_mid. Two different classes travel upward so neither level
| violates the one-handler-per-class rule:
|
|   test (level 0)  handles Ping
|   this file       handles Pong, and asks base for Ping
|   base_chain_mid  asks base for Pong
|
| Each `to base` must land exactly one level up — never skipping to the root,
| never falling through to a grandparent.
Pong { value } =>
    return Pong { value = value + 10 }

link "base_chain_mid"

emit Ping { value = 1 } to base get got
assert got.value = 11
